# Shell scripts must be LF. A CRLF shebang line makes the kernel look for an
# interpreter named "bash\r", which fails with the useless message
# "bad interpreter: No such file or directory" — a loud failure, but a misleading
# one. Authored on Windows, run on Linux; pin it here rather than relying on
# every contributor's core.autocrlf.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
